        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Elements got transported into the physical world! Will you be the hero to defeat them? Well… No. <i><strong>You are the Elements!</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After a breach mysteriously opened in the elemental world, Air, Fire, Stone and Water explore this new land and discover concepts they would never have imagined - such as &quot;<i>forests</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>tides&quot;</i> or even &quot;<i>people</i>&quot;</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Game mechanics</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Wisps of the Elements</i></strong> is a grid-based rogue-lite. Each element has a special effect: Fire and Stone aim at controlling the board, while Air and Water get bonuses and penalties depending on the tide cycle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies are matched at random, ensuring that each group of opponents is unique. With every expedition comes a new choice of spells; build powerful synergies or you'll be easily countered. Will you be outsmarted by an AI?</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Looking for a good challenge?</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Wisps of the Elements</i></strong> is difficult by design. There is no xp nor equipment to increase your stats - only your logic and knowledge of the game. The enemies all have unique abilities, and an AI smart enough to use them in synergy. So… still interested?</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The Elements got transported into the physical world! Will you be the hero to defeat them? Well… No. <i><strong>You are the Elements!</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After a breach mysteriously opened in the elemental world, Air, Fire, Stone and Water explore this new land and discover concepts they would never have imagined - such as &quot;<i>forests</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>tides&quot;</i> or even &quot;<i>people</i>&quot;</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Game mechanics</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Wisps of the Elements</i></strong> is a grid-based rogue-lite. Each element has a special effect: Fire and Stone aim at controlling the board, while Air and Water get bonuses and penalties depending on the tide cycle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Enemies are matched at random, ensuring that each group of opponents is unique. With every expedition comes a new choice of spells; build powerful synergies or you'll be easily countered. Will you be outsmarted by an AI?</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Looking for a good challenge?</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Wisps of the Elements</i></strong> is difficult by design. There is no xp nor equipment to increase your stats - only your logic and knowledge of the game. The enemies all have unique abilities, and an AI smart enough to use them in synergy. So… still interested?</p>",
        "short_description": "Guide Air, Fire, Stone, and Water through a grid-based rogue-lite, in which every spell can have a huge impact. Your enemies are smart enough to anticipate your moves and exploit their own synergies - can your tactics turn the tide?",
